            <ArticleTitle>[Phosphocreatine: thrombocyte aggregation in patients with stenocardia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Phosphocreatine (Neoton produced by &quot;Schapparelli Farmaceutici&quot;) was infused intravenously to 27 patients with CHD at a dose of 2000 mg: 13 patients with unstable and 10 patients with stable angina pectoris. Phosphocreatine blocked ADP-induced platelet aggregation in these patients, but had no significant effect on the platelet aggregation induced by collagen, platelet activating factor or serotonin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
